      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "Epiphysiodesis has become one of the most popular methods in the treatment of leg length discrepancy (LLD) due to its surgical simplicity, short hospitalization time, and a low risk of complications."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS AND METHODS",
          "content": "A retrospective analysis was performed on 34 patients treated for LDD with percutaneus epiphisiodesis of the distal femur and/or the proximal tibia. The mean discrepancy was 2.8 cm. The outcome evaluation method was based on Kemnitz et al."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Based on the Kemnitz criteria, 23 (67.6%) patients experienced good results, while 2 (5.9%) satisfactory and 9 (26.5%) poor results. In 47% of patients, swellings of the knee joint were observed in the postoperative period. One serious complication - varus deformity of 10 degrees in femur occurred in the follow-up period."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Percutaneous epiphysiodesis is a simple method of the LLD correction, with a low rate of complications and applicable in cases of late LDD diagnosis."
        }
      ]},
